OpenWings patch 0023: Lichen, the default look, and nothing of upstream's look under it

Lichen (theme key ow-sage) is a mid-tone sage look in one mode for
everyone: moss ink, one deep ochre accent, Sofia Sans, no dark variant.
Its stylesheet, design tokens and motion live in wings/brand/ (looks/
sage.css, tokens.css, tokens.json, motion.js); this patch wires them in
and keeps upstream's own look out of sight while any OpenWings look is on.

  * static/js/theme.js: Lichen in THEMES (first) with the display name
    Lichen; it is the default with nothing saved, and as a one-mode look
    it never gets a -night suffix. The theme picker lists only the
    OpenWings looks (Lichen, Duet, Duet night, Hush, Hush night); upstream's
    themes stay in the code, a saved one keeps working and stays listed
    while it is active, and all of them are listed when the deployment
    sets WINGS_SHOW_CLASSIC_THEMES=1. static/js/slashCommands.js: /theme
    and /setup theme list the same names.
  * src/app_helpers.py, static/index.html: the server fills index.html's
    data-ow-classic-themes from WINGS_SHOW_CLASSIC_THEMES.
  * static/index.html, static/login.html: the boot scripts default to
    Lichen; skins.css is a parser-inserted stylesheet (it holds the first
    layout; it has its own cache-bust token, owlooks<N>, used by every page
    that links it and by static/sw.js PRECACHE, bumped with CACHE_NAME when
    a look changes), and Fira Code is preloaded only for an upstream
    theme, so no upstream font is requested under a look. index.html loads
    /static/openwings/motion.js (defer), which does nothing under any
    other theme. Both pages, and static/manifest.json (the installed
    app's splash and title bar), use Lichen's page colour #C7CFC1 as the
    theme colour instead of upstream's dark slate. login.html: "Remember
    me" is a labelled row under the password, not an unlabelled dot.
  * static/js/theme.js: the look swatches are a radio group the keyboard
    can reach (Tab to the current look, arrows to move, Enter or Space to
    wear one); the locked Customize fields show the look's accent and
    light or dark mode, not upstream's red and Dark.
  * Pages outside the app shell wear the look (static/openwings/look.js or
    the same inline line marks it before the first paint): the web search
    results page (routes/search/search_routes.py, still one nonce'd
    script) and the MCP sign-in result page (routes/mcp/mcp_routes.py).
  * Things upstream colours by category take the look's palette
    (--ow-palette and --ow-tints in each look): calendar tags, calendars
    left on upstream's default blue, the event colour swatches and the
    custom swatch (static/js/calendar.js, calendar/utils.js), and Cookbook
    servers without a colour of their own (static/js/cookbook.js).
  * static/js/chatRenderer.js, static/js/chat.js: a model route reads
    "mock-beta (Selected route → Mock)" with the arrow kept with its word,
    and a tool without a label of its own shows its name in words
    ("Draft email", not "mcp__email__draft_email").
  * static/js/spinner.js: under a look, the whirlpool and sine-wave
    canvases and the ASCII wave become one neutral mark (three dots that
    breathe, styled in skins.css, which also hides the ASCII waves the
    chat, compaction, Compare, Cookbook and the start-up loader write).
    Upstream themes keep upstream's spinners.
  * src/theme_palette.py, src/ai_interaction.py, src/agent_loop.py,
    src/tool_schemas.py: ow-sage is a known preset and the default the
    model is told about; set_theme also takes the picker's names (Lichen,
    Duet, Duet night, Hush, Hush night); static/js/theme.js
    resolveThemeName does the same for the slash commands (patch 0024).

Applies to: odysseus-dev/odysseus@9d0d3720f4ca181d87bef94da826d730acc6d483
